# The Search and Type Index Services (lws10-index) (YAML-LD).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: LWS Search and Type Index Services
comment: >-
  lws10-index is an editor's draft that W3C has not published; its requirements are catalogued
  as Draft from a snapshot rendered on 2026-10-02 (D-0067). Each test applies when the storage
  advertises the service it exercises. Resources declare types unique to the test both ways a
  server may read them: a Link rel=type on the creating POST (servers SHOULD derive types from
  it) and the Turtle body (they MAY). A test that needs a typed resource first waits for the
  search to surface it, as a precondition, so a server that derives no declared type makes it
  inapplicable rather than failed; two tests report each derivation on its own. Index
  membership may be eventually consistent, so a step that waits for a resource to appear is
  polled; authorization filtering may not, so a step after a revocation is not.
specification:
  - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/
entries:

  - id: "#index-services-advertised"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: index-services-advertised
    label: Each advertised Type Index or Type Search Service has a serviceEndpoint
    comment: >-
      A storage "MAY support the Type Index Service, the Type Search Service, or both", and one
       that does "MUST advertise it with a service object" of type TypeIndexService or
       TypeSearchService, and "Each service object MUST include a serviceEndpoint". Applies when
       the storage description advertises either service.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#discovery
    traits: [Get, StorageDescription, Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/services-optional
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/service-advertised
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/service-endpoint
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Index or Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  matches: "^Type(Index|Search)Service$"
      - label: every such service object names its endpoint
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              none:
                - pointer: /type
                  matches: "^Type(Index|Search)Service$"
                - pointer: /serviceEndpoint
                  exists: false
            - pointer: /service
              none:
                - pointer: /type
                  matches: "^Type(Index|Search)Service$"
                - pointer: /serviceEndpoint
                  jsonType: object

  - id: "#type-index-lists-readable-types"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-index-lists-readable-types
    label: The type index lists a type borne by a resource the client may read
    comment: >-
      bob may read a resource whose Turtle declares a type unique to this test. bob's GET of the
       TypeIndexService answers a TypeIndex in application/lws+json that lists that type (polled:
       membership "MAY be eventually consistent"). Types a server takes from content "MUST be
       treated identically" to those from Link headers.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-index-get
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/authorization-enforced
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/content-types-identical
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-content
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: visible
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Index Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeIndexService
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: alice's search finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${visible}"
      - label: bob's type index lists the type
        as: bob
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${service.TypeIndexService}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              equals: TypeIndex
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${test.container}#Alpha"

  - id: "#type-index-omits-unreadable-type"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-index-omits-unreadable-type
    label: The type index omits a type borne only by resources the client may not read
    comment: >-
      Two resources declare types unique to this test: bob may read the one of type Alpha, not
       the one of type Beta. Once alice's search finds the Beta resource (so it is indexed) and
       bob's type index lists Alpha, bob's type index must not list Beta: "Unauthorized entries
       MUST be omitted entirely", and no response may reveal "that a specific type exists in the
       storage at all" without the authorization.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-index-get
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unauthorized-omitted
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-existence-disclosure
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/authorization-enforced
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: visible
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
        - dataResource: hidden
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Beta> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Beta"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Index Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeIndexService
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: alice's search finds the Beta resource (it is indexed) (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Beta"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${hidden}"
      - label: bob's type index lists Alpha, and not Beta
        as: bob
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${service.TypeIndexService}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${test.container}#Beta"

  - id: "#type-index-not-shared"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-index-not-shared
    label: A type index response is marked against reuse across clients
    comment: >-
      The type index is authorization-filtered, so "A server MUST mark such responses so that
       they are not reused across clients (for example with Cache-Control: private or no-store)".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/responses-private
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-shared-cache
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Index Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeIndexService
      - label: the type index is Cache-Control private or no-store
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${service.TypeIndexService}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Cache-Control
              matches: "(?i)\\b(private|no-store)\\b"

  - id: "#type-search-by-type"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-by-type
    label: A search on one type returns a ContainerPage with the resource that bears it
    comment: >-
      A resource declares two types unique to this test. A QUERY in application/lws-query+json
       (the baseline every server "MUST support") on one of them, with no Accept, returns 200 and
       an application/lws+json ContainerPage whose items include the resource, carrying "at least
       the matched resource's id and its type". Polled: membership "MAY be eventually
       consistent".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Conneg]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/baseline-format-supported
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-key-supported
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/search-default-containerpage
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/result-item-id-type
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-filter
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/content-types-identical
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-content
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha>, <${test.container}#Beta> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Beta"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: search for Alpha finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: search for Alpha, with no Accept, answers a ContainerPage whose item has the resource's id and type
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              equals: ContainerPage
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: "${test.container}#Alpha"

  - id: "#type-search-and-or"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-and-or
    label: Type groups are ANDed and the IRIs inside a group ORed
    comment: >-
      The type value "is an array whose elements are combined with logical AND; each element is
       either a single type IRI or an array of type IRIs combined with logical OR". Three resources
       of types {Alpha, Beta}, {Alpha} and {Gamma}: [[Alpha, Gamma]] finds all three; [Alpha, Beta]
       only the first; [[Beta, Gamma], Alpha] only the first.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-filter
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-key-supported
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha>, <${test.container}#Beta> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Beta"
        - dataResource: two
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: three
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Gamma> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Gamma"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[[Alpha, Gamma]] finds all three (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - ["${test.container}#Alpha", "${test.container}#Gamma"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${three}"
      - label: "[Alpha, Beta] finds only the resource with both"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha", "${test.container}#Beta"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${three}"
      - label: "[[Beta, Gamma], Alpha] finds only the first"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - ["${test.container}#Beta", "${test.container}#Gamma"]
              - "${test.container}#Alpha"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${three}"

  - id: "#type-search-native-classes"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-native-classes
    label: lws:DataResource and lws:Container filter on what the resource itself is
    comment: >-
      "The native LWS classes https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#DataResource and
       https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#Container are ordinary type values: filtering on them selects
       resources that are themselves data resources or containers". A data resource of type Alpha
       matches [Alpha, lws:DataResource] and not [Alpha, lws:Container].
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, DataResource]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-filter
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-key-supported
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-link-headers
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha, lws:DataResource] finds it (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha", "https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#DataResource"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha, lws:Container] does not"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha", "https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#Container"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-no-match"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-no-match
    label: A type that matches nothing yields an empty result, not an error
    comment: >-
      "A type IRI that matches no resource yields no results and MUST NOT be treated as an
       error." The type is unique to this test, so nothing bears it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-match-not-error
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/search-default-containerpage
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: search for a type nothing bears
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              count: 0

  - id: "#type-search-duplicate-groups"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-duplicate-groups
    label: Duplicate groups in a filter are ignored
    comment: >-
      "duplicate groups MUST be ignored": [Alpha, Alpha, [Alpha]] selects what [Alpha] does.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/duplicate-groups-ignored
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha, Alpha, [Alpha]] finds it too"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - "${test.container}#Alpha"
              - "${test.container}#Alpha"
              - ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-at-members-ignored"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-at-members-ignored
    label: Filter members whose names begin with @ are ignored
    comment: >-
      "A member whose name begins with @ (a JSON-LD keyword such as @context) MUST be ignored; it
       is neither a constraint nor a relation key." A filter with @context and @type beside
       type [Alpha] finds the Alpha resource.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/at-members-ignored
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha] with @context and @type members finds the resource"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1
            "@type": urn:touchstone:not-a-filter
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-empty-key-absent"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-empty-key-absent
    label: A filter key whose whole value is an empty array is no constraint
    comment: >-
      A key whose value is an empty array "expresses no constraint and is treated as if the key
       were absent", and a body whose keys all have empty arrays "matches all resources visible to
       the client". type [Alpha] with describedby [] finds the Alpha resource.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-filter
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha] with an empty describedby finds the resource"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: []
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-empty-group-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-empty-group-rejected
    label: An empty group is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      "An empty group — an empty array appearing as an element of a filter key's value — MUST be
       rejected with 400 (Bad Request)", not ignored.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/empty-group-rejected
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/malformed-filter-400
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: type [[]] is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - []
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-type-not-array-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-type-not-array-rejected
    label: A type that is not an array is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      A body "whose type is not an array ... MUST be rejected with 400 (Bad Request)".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/malformed-filter-400
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: type as a bare string is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-bad-element-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-bad-element-rejected
    label: A type element that is not a string or array of strings is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      A body any of whose elements "is neither a string nor a non-empty array of strings, MUST be
       rejected with 400 (Bad Request)": a number, a group holding a number, and an object, the shape
       an extension of the grammar (which "a server MUST NOT" make) would take.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/malformed-filter-400
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/grammar-not-extended
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: type [42] is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: [42]
        response:
          statusCode: 400
      - label: type [[Alpha, 7]] is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - ["${test.container}#Alpha", 7]
        response:
          statusCode: 400
      - label: "type [{not: Alpha}] is refused"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - not: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-malformed-json-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-malformed-json-rejected
    label: A body that is not well-formed JSON is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      "A request body that is not well-formed application/lws-query+json ... MUST be rejected
       with 400 (Bad Request)".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/malformed-filter-400
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: an unterminated JSON body is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          body: '{"type": ["urn:touchstone:a"'
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-relative-iri-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-relative-iri-rejected
    label: A type or relation value that is not an absolute IRI is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      "A type value, or any relation target value, that does not match the IRI production of
       [RFC3987] ... MUST be rejected with 400 (Bad Request)". This is distinct from a well-formed
       IRI that matches nothing.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/invalid-iri-400
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: type [Person] is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["Person"]
        response:
          statusCode: 400
      - label: a describedby target with spaces and no scheme is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            describedby: ["not an iri"]
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-missing-content-type-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-missing-content-type-rejected
    label: A search without a Content-Type is rejected with 400
    comment: >-
      "A request that omits the Content-Type header field, which [RFC10008] requires a server to
       reject, MUST be rejected with 400 (Bad Request)." The body is a valid filter.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/missing-content-type-400
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/query-content-type-required
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: a QUERY with no Content-Type is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          body: '{"type": ["urn:touchstone:nothing"]}'
        response:
          statusCode: 400

  - id: "#type-search-unsupported-format-rejected"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-unsupported-format-rejected
    label: A search in an unsupported query format is rejected with 415
    comment: >-
      "A request whose Content-Type identifies a query format the server does not support MUST be
       rejected with 415 (Unsupported Media Type)." The format is one no LWS server is required to
       support, a made-up media type.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unsupported-format-415
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: a QUERY in application/x-touchstone-query is refused
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/x-touchstone-query
          body: '{"type": ["urn:touchstone:nothing"]}'
        response:
          statusCode: 415

  - id: "#type-search-unsupported-format-accept-query"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-unsupported-format-accept-query
    label: A 415 from the search lists the accepted formats in Accept-Query
    comment: >-
      A 415 response "SHOULD include an Accept-Query header field [RFC10008] listing the query
       formats the server does accept", and every server accepts application/lws-query+json.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unsupported-format-accept-query
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: the 415 carries Accept-Query naming application/lws-query+json
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/x-touchstone-query
          body: '{"type": ["urn:touchstone:nothing"]}'
        response:
          statusCode: 415
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Accept-Query
              matches: "(?i)application/lws-query\\+json"

  - id: "#type-search-accept-query-advertised"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-accept-query-advertised
    label: OPTIONS on the search endpoint advertises its query formats in Accept-Query
    comment: >-
      "A server SHOULD advertise the query formats it accepts using the Accept-Query response
       header field — for example in response to an OPTIONS request on the service endpoint", and
       Accept-Query "enumerates only the query-format media types": every entry is a media type.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/accept-query-advertised
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/accept-query-no-disclosure
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: OPTIONS names application/lws-query+json in Accept-Query, and nothing but media types
        request:
          method: OPTIONS
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Accept-Query
              matches: "(?i)application/lws-query\\+json"
            - headerName: Accept-Query
              matches: "^\\s*[A-Za-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]+/[A-Za-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]+(\\s*;[^,]*)?(\\s*,\\s*[A-Za-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]+/[A-Za-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]+(\\s*;[^,]*)?)*\\s*$"

  - id: "#type-search-not-acceptable"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: type-search-not-acceptable
    label: A search whose Accept excludes every format the server can produce is rejected with 406
    comment: >-
      "A request whose Accept header field excludes every response media type the server can
       produce for the result set MUST be rejected with 406", and since every server produces the
       lws+json ContainerPage, one that admits it "never results in 406".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/not-acceptable-406
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/search-default-containerpage
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "Accept: image/png is refused"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          accept: "image/png"
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 406
      - label: Accept admitting application/lws+json at low weight is answered
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          accept: "image/png, application/lws+json;q=0.1"
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json

  - id: "#type-search-unindexed-relation"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-unindexed-relation
    label: An unindexed relation and an unmatched relation target both yield an empty result
    comment: >-
      "A relation the server does not index, like a target value that matches nothing, yields no
       results for that constraint: this MUST NOT be treated as an error, and the two cases MUST be
       indistinguishable to the client." Beside type [Alpha], which finds the resource, a relation
       no server indexes and a describedby target nothing declares both give 200 with no items.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unindexed-relation-indistinguishable
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/relations-may-be-indexed
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-match-not-error
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] alone finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: with a relation nobody indexes, nothing
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            "urn:touchstone:unindexed-relation": ["urn:touchstone:x"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              count: 0
      - label: with a describedby target nothing declares, nothing
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["urn:touchstone:no-such-shape"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              count: 0

  - id: "#type-search-structural-relation-not-indexed"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-structural-relation-not-indexed
    label: A structural relation such as up is not indexed
    comment: >-
      "servers MUST NOT index structural or protocol relations", so a filter on up yields no
       results, as for any relation the server does not index — even naming the container the
       Alpha resource is in.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Container]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/structural-relations-not-indexed
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unindexed-relation-indistinguishable
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] alone finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha] with up naming its container finds nothing"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            up: ["${test.container}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              count: 0

  - id: "#type-search-authorization-filtered"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-authorization-filtered
    label: A search omits resources the client may not read, and counts only those it may
    comment: >-
      Two resources of type Alpha; bob may read one. Once alice's search finds both, bob's
       search finds the one he may read and not the other: "Unauthorized entries MUST be omitted
       entirely", and a totalItems, if given, "MUST be computed over this client-specific,
       authorization-filtered view".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
    traits: [Discovery, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/unauthorized-omitted
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-existence-disclosure
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/authorization-enforced
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/counts-filtered
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/derived-index-filtered
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: visible
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
        - dataResource: hidden
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: alice's search finds both (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${visible}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${hidden}"
      - label: bob's search finds only the one he may read, and counts one
        as: bob
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${visible}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${hidden}"
            - pointer: /totalItems
              optional: true
              equals: 1

  - id: "#type-search-revoked-not-shown"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-revoked-not-shown
    label: Once a grant is revoked, the search stops returning what it gave access to
    comment: >-
      bob finds a resource through a grant; alice revokes it. "Once an authorization (such as an
       access grant) is revoked or narrowed, the affected types and resource URIs MUST NOT appear
       in any subsequent response": the very next search must omit it, since "the
       eventual-consistency allowance ... MUST NOT be extended to authorization".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Authz, AccessGrants, Delete]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/revoked-not-shown
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/current-authorization
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/consistency-not-for-authorization
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/derived-index-filtered
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: target
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: grant bob read on the resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${target}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: with the grant, bob's search finds it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        as: bob
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${target}"
      - label: alice revokes the grant
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${grant}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: bob can no longer read the resource (otherwise revocation did not take effect, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${target}"
        response:
          statusCode: [401, 403, 404]
      - label: bob's next search omits it
        as: bob
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${target}"

  - id: "#type-search-not-shared"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-not-shared
    label: A search response is marked against reuse across clients
    comment: >-
      A QUERY response is cacheable, yet authorization-filtered, so "A server MUST mark such
       responses so that they are not reused across clients (for example with Cache-Control:
       private or no-store)".
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#security-authorization
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/responses-private
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-shared-cache
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: the search response is Cache-Control private or no-store
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Cache-Control
              matches: "(?i)\\b(private|no-store)\\b"

  - id: "#type-search-type-from-link-header"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-type-from-link-header
    label: A type declared only by Link rel=type on create is searchable
    comment: >-
      "servers SHOULD derive resource types from HTTP Link headers provided by the client during
       resource creation or modification". A text/plain resource created with a Link rel=type
       naming a type unique to this test is found by a search on that type.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Post]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-link-headers
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: linked
          contentType: text/plain
          body: typed only by its Link header
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: search for Alpha finds it
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${linked}"

  - id: "#type-search-type-from-content"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-type-from-content
    label: A type declared only in the resource's Turtle is searchable
    comment: >-
      "Servers MAY additionally derive types from the resource representation itself when they
       are able to parse it", and such types "MUST be treated identically". A Turtle resource
       stating <> a Alpha, with no Link header, is found by a search on Alpha.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Post]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-content
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/content-types-identical
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: typed
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: search for Alpha finds it
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${typed}"

  - id: "#type-search-reflects-update"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-reflects-update
    label: After an update changes a resource's types, the search follows
    comment: >-
      "Following a write that changes a resource's derivable types ... (creation, update, or
       deletion), a server SHOULD reflect the change within a bounded, implementation-defined
       interval." A resource of type Alpha is replaced (both by Link rel=type and in its Turtle) by
       one of type Beta: a search on Beta comes to find it, and one on Alpha comes to omit it.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Put]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-link-headers
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-content
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: replace it with a resource of type Beta
        request:
          method: PUT
          url: "${one}"
          ifMatch: current
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Beta> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Beta"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: "[Beta] comes to find it"
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Beta"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha] comes to omit it"
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-reflects-delete"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-reflects-delete
    label: After a resource is deleted, the search stops returning it
    comment: >-
      A deletion is one of the writes a server "SHOULD reflect ... within a bounded,
       implementation-defined interval": once the Alpha resource is deleted, a search on Alpha
       comes to omit it.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Delete]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/reflect-change-bounded
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: delete it
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${one}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: "[Alpha] comes to omit it"
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-vary-accept"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-vary-accept
    label: A search that negotiates its response format lists Accept in Vary
    comment: >-
      "A server that negotiates the response representation on Accept ... MUST list Accept in
       Vary so that caches do not reuse a representation across response formats." Applies when
       the search answers Accept: application/ld+json in that format; then both that response and
       the default lws+json one vary on Accept.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Conneg]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/vary-accept
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/other-response-formats
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: the search answers application/ld+json when asked (otherwise it does not negotiate, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          accept: "application/ld+json"
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/ld+json
      - label: the ld+json response lists Accept in Vary
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          accept: "application/ld+json"
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Vary
              matches: "(?i)(^|[\\s,])(accept|\\*)([\\s,]|$)"
      - label: the default response lists Accept in Vary
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Nothing"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Vary
              matches: "(?i)(^|[\\s,])(accept|\\*)([\\s,]|$)"

  - id: "#type-search-safe"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-safe
    label: A search changes nothing, and repeating it gives the same result
    comment: >-
      "The QUERY method is both safe and idempotent: a search never alters server state, and
       it MAY be repeated". Around two identical searches, the resource and its container keep
       their ETags, and both searches find the resource.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Conditional]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/query-safe-idempotent
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: note the resource's ETag
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${one}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              capture: resourceEtag
      - label: note the container's ETag
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              capture: containerEtag
      - label: search once
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: search again, with the same result
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: the resource's ETag is unchanged
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${one}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              headerValue: "${resourceEtag}"
      - label: the container's ETag is unchanged
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              headerValue: "${containerEtag}"

  - id: "#type-search-next-page"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-next-page
    label: Following a search result's rel=next yields the rest of the same result set
    comment: >-
      Search results are "paginated according to the standard LWS pagination model ... page URIs
       are conveyed in Link headers ... and are dereferenced to retrieve subsequent pages". Five
       resources share type Alpha; when the search splits them into pages, the next page is 200
       lws+json, holds only Alpha resources, and does not repeat page one's first item. Applies
       when the server's page holds fewer than five.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Get]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/search-default-containerpage
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/result-item-id-type
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/pagination-link-first
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: m1
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: m2
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: m3
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: m4
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: m5
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha>, <${test.container}#Epsilon> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Epsilon"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: the last-created resource is found (so all five are indexed) (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Epsilon"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${m5}"
      - label: the search on Alpha spans pages (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: next
      - label: read the first page, keeping its next link and its first item
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: next
              capture: next
          json:
            - pointer: /items/0/id
              capture: firstItem
      - label: the next page holds more Alpha resources, not page one's first
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${next}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              equals: ContainerPage
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  jsonType: string
            - pointer: /items
              every:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - pointer: /items
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${firstItem}"

  - id: "#type-search-relation-filter"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-relation-filter
    label: A describedby link in a resource's linkset can be searched on
    comment: >-
      "A server MAY additionally index other descriptive link relations. Such a relation is
       filtered by using the relation itself as a key alongside type". An Alpha resource whose
       linkset gains describedby a shape is found by type [Alpha] and describedby [shape]. A server
       that does not index describedby fails this MAY.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Linkset, Patch]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/relations-may-be-indexed
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: find the linkset of ${one}
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${one}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: add describedby ShapeOne to ${one} through its linkset (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          ifMatch: current
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${one}"
                describedby:
                  - href: "${test.container}#ShapeOne"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: "[Alpha] with describedby [shape] finds it"
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["${test.container}#ShapeOne"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"

  - id: "#type-search-relation-cnf"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-relation-cnf
    label: "Relation values combine like type values: groups ANDed, nested arrays ORed"
    comment: >-
      An indexed relation is filtered "with exactly the same conjunctive-normal-form semantics as
       type (a nested array is an OR group, sibling array elements form AND groups ...)". Two Alpha
       resources are describedby shape one and shape two, through their linksets: describedby
       [[one, two]] finds both, and describedby [one, two] finds neither. Applies when the server
       indexes describedby.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery, Linkset, Patch]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/relations-may-be-indexed
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/type-filter
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
        - dataResource: two
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds both resources (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"
      - label: find the linkset of ${one}
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${one}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linksetOne
      - label: add describedby ShapeOne to ${one} through its linkset (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linksetOne}"
          ifMatch: current
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${one}"
                describedby:
                  - href: "${test.container}#ShapeOne"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: find the linkset of ${two}
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${two}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linksetTwo
      - label: add describedby ShapeTwo to ${two} through its linkset (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linksetTwo}"
          ifMatch: current
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${two}"
                describedby:
                  - href: "${test.container}#ShapeTwo"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: describedby [shape one] finds the first (otherwise describedby is not indexed, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["${test.container}#ShapeOne"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: describedby [[shape one, shape two]] finds both
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby:
              - ["${test.container}#ShapeOne", "${test.container}#ShapeTwo"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"
      - label: describedby [shape one, shape two] finds neither
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["${test.container}#ShapeOne", "${test.container}#ShapeTwo"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
            - pointer: /items
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${two}"

  - id: "#type-search-relation-from-link-header"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-relation-from-link-header
    label: A describedby link sent as a Link header on create is searchable like one in the linkset
    comment: >-
      Relation targets "are derived by the server in the same way as types (HTTP Link headers,
       server-intrinsic state, or parsed content) and all sources MUST be treated identically", and
       types SHOULD be derived from the Link headers of a create. One Alpha resource gains describedby
       a shape through its linkset; another declares the same link as a Link header when it is
       created. Once the first is found by describedby [shape], the second should be too. Applies
       when the server indexes describedby.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-derivation
    traits: [Discovery, Linkset, Post]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/relation-sources-identical
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/types-from-link-headers
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/relations-may-be-indexed
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: linked
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
            - rel: describedby
              href: "${test.container}#ShapeOne"
        - dataResource: patched
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds both resources (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${linked}"
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${patched}"
      - label: find the linkset of ${patched}
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${patched}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: add describedby ShapeOne to ${patched} through its linkset (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          ifMatch: current
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${patched}"
                describedby:
                  - href: "${test.container}#ShapeOne"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: describedby [shape] finds the linkset resource (otherwise describedby is not indexed, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["${test.container}#ShapeOne"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${patched}"
      - label: describedby [shape] comes to find the Link-header resource too
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
            describedby: ["${test.container}#ShapeOne"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${linked}"

  - id: "#type-search-too-complex"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: type-search-too-complex
    label: A filter beyond the server's limit is refused with 422, never narrowed
    comment: >-
      A filter "that is well-formed but exceeds the complexity a server chooses to support ...
       MUST be rejected with 422", and "A server MUST NOT silently truncate or otherwise narrow such a
       filter". Type [Alpha] followed by 99 types nothing bears matches nothing: the server either
       refuses it with 422 or answers 200 without the Alpha resource. A server that dropped the
       groups past its limit would return it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/too-complex-422
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/no-silent-narrowing
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: one
          contentType: text/turtle
          body: "<> a <${test.container}#Alpha> ."
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: type
              href: "${test.container}#Alpha"
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers a Type Search Service (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: TypeSearchService
      - label: "[Alpha] finds the resource (otherwise the server derives no declared type, and this test does not apply)"
        precondition: true
        poll: {within: 60, every: 3}
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type: ["${test.container}#Alpha"]
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${one}"
      - label: "[Alpha, 99 types nothing bears] is refused with 422 or answered without it"
        request:
          method: QUERY
          url: "${service.TypeSearchService}"
          contentType: application/lws-query+json
          bodyJSON:
            type:
              - "${test.container}#Alpha"
              - "${test.container}#None-1"
              - "${test.container}#None-2"
              - "${test.container}#None-3"
              - "${test.container}#None-4"
              - "${test.container}#None-5"
              - "${test.container}#None-6"
              - "${test.container}#None-7"
              - "${test.container}#None-8"
              - "${test.container}#None-9"
              - "${test.container}#None-10"
              - "${test.container}#None-11"
              - "${test.container}#None-12"
              - "${test.container}#None-13"
              - "${test.container}#None-14"
              - "${test.container}#None-15"
              - "${test.container}#None-16"
              - "${test.container}#None-17"
              - "${test.container}#None-18"
              - "${test.container}#None-19"
              - "${test.container}#None-20"
              - "${test.container}#None-21"
              - "${test.container}#None-22"
              - "${test.container}#None-23"
              - "${test.container}#None-24"
              - "${test.container}#None-25"
              - "${test.container}#None-26"
              - "${test.container}#None-27"
              - "${test.container}#None-28"
              - "${test.container}#None-29"
              - "${test.container}#None-30"
              - "${test.container}#None-31"
              - "${test.container}#None-32"
